    "description": "Virginia Mineral & Rock Collection\n20 Mounted Geological Specimens with Identification Chart\nFrom the Collection of Rudolph J. Bland, Jr.\nAuthentic boxed collection of 20 mineral and rock specimens representing various counties across the Commonwealth of Virginia. Assembled from the collection of noted Virginia mineralogist Rudolph J. Bland, Jr., this educational reference set features an indexed label on the interior lid pairing each numbered specimen with its mineral type and county locality. Also includes a group of accompanying loose stones, a projectile point, and a seashell.\nContains 20 Virginia specimens including amazonite, amethyst, staurolite, unakite, prehnite, and petrified wood\nInterior lid index clearly lists specimen identity and Virginia county of origin\nMounted in compartmentalized cardboard presentation mailer box\nIncludes additional loose pieces: projectile point, tumbled stones, and seashell\nMeasures 11.5 x 8 x 2.75 inches\nCondition:\nAll 20 numbered specimen compartments retain their original mounted mineral samples. Interior lid chart is complete and legible. Exterior box shows surface age toning, handling wear, and spotting on the lid. Loose accent stones and artifact point are intact.\nPlease Note:\nThis is a pre-owned item being sold\nas-is\n. We do our best to describe items accurately and include research where possible, but we are not experts in every category. Please note that if the title or description states \"Tested\" that we only test to make sure the unit \"\nPOWERS ON\"\n.\nNo further testing takes place unless stated otherwise and items are considered untested.\nPlease remember all items are used and are sold as is, no refunds.If you have questions, please contact us before bidding.\nFor all vintage clothing, please research sizing before placing a bid.\nItems from different time periods may have measurements that differ from today’s standard sizing.\nCustomer Service:\nReach us via the “Contact Us” link above or by calling\n(540) 361-6550\n. Messages are handled Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:00 PM ET, and we strive to respond within 48 hours.",
