    "description": "Petrified Wood Specimens\nNatural Fossilized Wood Lot\nSet of 3 Pieces\nThis collection features three distinct pieces of natural petrified wood displaying unique mineralized grain patterns and organic textures. Petrified wood forms over millions of years through permineralization, where organic wood material is replaced by silicate minerals while retaining the original cellular structure. These specimen pieces offer excellent aesthetic appeal for display, geological study, or natural decor.\nItems Included:\nOne elongated dark specimen with prominent weathered bark texture and white mineral accents\nOne smooth, rounded oval specimen featuring visible wood grain and light tan coloration\nOne rounded cylindrical piece with weathered grain striations in neutral driftwood tones\nCondition:\nNatural rough and weathered specimen condition. Each piece retains organic edges, natural mineral striations, and surface fissures consistent with fossilization and natural weathering. No artificial alterations, cracks from impact, or post-extraction damage observed.",
